**Since the previous report:** Fixed an Accounting entitlement bypass in manual posting. Server action and transaction now enforce writable grants; transaction-held authority rows coordinate with module changes. A final check catches grant expiry during preparation. Stopping creation alone still permits an existing draft's authorized completion. Denial retains an audit without financial effects; failed authority reads cannot grant access.

**Verification:** 196 tests/10 suites, full no-emit TypeScript and four-file lint passed; 9 owned PostgreSQL scenarios passed with stable bound source and observed outside-fixture state. These are authority-boundary checks, not an overall completion percentage. No new browser/EN-FR/accessibility proof is claimed. [Correction, verification and operating guide](MANUAL_POSTING_MODULE_AUTHORITY_2026-10-01.md); [independent review](MANUAL_POSTING_MODULE_REVIEW_2026-10-01.md).

**Unchanged blocker:** Earlier-period Close certification invalidation remains incomplete. The prior actual-database run had seven passes and two failures; those failures are retained, not relabeled. Its raw source binding is now historical where posting changed. Automatic approval review rejected the all-period helper twice for contention risk; it remains unapplied pending explicit user approval. [Exact proposal](MANUAL_POSTING_SCOPE_REVIEW_2026-10-01.md).

**Remaining:** Complete producer scope, draft-created snapshot freshness, purchase-specific recovery, role/session revocation guarantees, interrupted processing and outbox delivery. Full journal UI localization/accessibility, genuine country/payroll prerequisites and production capacity remain open. Grant validity is checked after preparation, not guaranteed against expiry during later SQL waits at eventual commit.

All 17 original workflow families and their backlog remain in the [register](WORKFLOW_REGISTER.json). The other 268 rows, all families and statuses are unchanged. No migration, reset, deployment, live activation, customer payment, external message or X1 clearance occurred. The full goal remains active; an ETA is not reliable.
